1
00:00:05,087 --> 00:00:06,964
{\an8}I just have a couple more questions for you.

2
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:12,762
- Hey. Where's Lisbon?
- She's in court.

3
00:00:13,137 --> 00:00:14,305
You know you're late.

4
00:00:14,847 --> 00:00:18,100
Yeah, I must have turned
my alarm clock off. Overslept.

5
00:00:18,434 --> 00:00:19,685
Hot date?

6
00:00:23,022 --> 00:00:24,440
What are you talking about?

7
00:00:24,899 --> 00:00:27,527
Well, you know.
Duncan. From L.A.

8
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:32,448
- Wayne, it's not like that.
- Oh, right. Sure.

9
00:00:32,573 --> 00:00:33,991
You mind finishing up
these interviews?

10
00:00:36,994 --> 00:00:38,120
Hi.

11
00:00:40,873 --> 00:00:43,084
- That's it, sir.
- Thanks.

12
00:00:45,127 --> 00:00:47,463
Van Pelt's here now.
Is Jane coming?

13
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:48,965
I don't know. Call him.

14
00:01:00,893 --> 00:01:02,895
Hey, Rigsby.
What's going on?

15
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:05,106
Uh, you know we have
a case, right?

16
00:01:05,231 --> 00:01:06,482
Yeah. I heard.

17
00:01:06,607 --> 00:01:09,193
I'm, uh, kind of busy here,
so I'm not gonna make it.

18
00:01:10,027 --> 00:01:11,445
He's not gonna make it.

19
00:01:12,113 --> 00:01:15,950
- Yeah, but I'm happy to help.
- Help how?

20
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:19,745
Well, you two talk to me, and I'll listen.
You'll be my eyes and my ears.

21
00:01:20,454 --> 00:01:22,081
Okay, I'll put you on speaker.

22
00:01:22,790 --> 00:01:24,584
Cho. Tell Jane what we got.

23
00:01:25,167 --> 00:01:27,420
Housewife. Missy Roberts. 32.

24
00:01:27,545 --> 00:01:29,505
Maid found her
shot in the bathroom.

25
00:01:31,215 --> 00:01:35,177
Now, there's bullet holes in the hallway
and one in the closet door here.

26
00:01:35,344 --> 00:01:37,847
"So it looks like a fight started elsewhere
then she ran to the bathroom."

27
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:39,765
"Forensics recovered
9-millimeter casings."

28
00:01:39,890 --> 00:01:41,892
Eh, forensics.
Tell me about the body.

29
00:01:42,935 --> 00:01:46,272
Well, she's lying here
on the floor in gym clothes.

30
00:01:46,647 --> 00:01:49,859
She's been shot in the chest,
uh, once in the foot

31
00:01:49,984 --> 00:01:52,528
and there's two bullet holes
lodged in the ground

32
00:01:52,653 --> 00:01:54,655
so we're not dealing
with an expert marksman.

33
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:57,700
Well, maybe, maybe not.
Uh, what about the husband?

34
00:01:58,326 --> 00:02:00,036
"Yeah. Husband."

35
00:02:00,661 --> 00:02:03,247
Name's Kip. He runs a high-end
home electronics company.

36
00:02:03,372 --> 00:02:07,335
"He left town 2 days ago on some boondoggle
white-water rafting trip to Tahoe."

37
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:10,254
- Interesting. How did he take the news?
- "Well, he hasn't gotten it yet."

38
00:02:10,379 --> 00:02:13,215
His office says the rafting group will be
out of cell range for another day or so.

39
00:02:14,175 --> 00:02:17,845
- Describe to me the bedroom.
- Why?

40
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:21,557
Well, I want to understand their
relationship. A bedroom says a lot.

41
00:02:22,308 --> 00:02:23,351
Okay.

42
00:02:25,561 --> 00:02:27,355
All right, it's, uh...

43
00:02:27,855 --> 00:02:31,692
Cold, impersonal.
Tightly made bed.

44
00:02:31,859 --> 00:02:34,654
- "No pictures."
- Let's try the kitchen.

45
00:02:34,945 --> 00:02:36,155
Okay.

46
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:43,996
- Okay. What am I looking for?
- Tell me what's in the fridge.

47
00:02:45,998 --> 00:02:50,086
Butter, milk, eggs...
Baking stuff.

48
00:02:51,962 --> 00:02:53,881
Which makes sense,
because there are these

49
00:02:54,006 --> 00:02:56,217
awesome looking cupcakes
on the counter.

50
00:02:57,134 --> 00:02:59,428
They're, uh, red velvet, I think.

51
00:02:59,553 --> 00:03:01,263
Yeah. What else is in the fridge?

52
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:04,517
A bunch of diet shakes and soda.

53
00:03:05,810 --> 00:03:08,813
- Is the victim heavy?
- Oh, no, she's very thin.

54
00:03:08,938 --> 00:03:11,816
- What about Kip?
- I guess he's kind of chubby.

55
00:03:12,316 --> 00:03:15,152
But it looks like he sees
a personal trainer, though.

56
00:03:15,319 --> 00:03:17,446
Oh, this is not
a happy marriage.

57
00:03:17,613 --> 00:03:19,699
Kip's portly but fights it.

58
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:22,118
Missy is naturally thin
and a gourmet baker.

59
00:03:22,326 --> 00:03:25,579
He views her hobby
as a sabotage and resents it.

60
00:03:25,705 --> 00:03:30,042
"She views his dieting as a lack
of interest in her personal outlet."

61
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:32,086
You need to talk to Kip.

62
00:03:33,212 --> 00:03:34,755
He wants us to talk to Kip.

63
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:37,883
We can't
not until tomorrow.

64
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:41,345
"Oh, please, this is the last guy
who'd go on a white-water rafting trip."

65
00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:44,557
You don't hire a personal trainer
'cause you like strenuous activity.

66
00:03:44,682 --> 00:03:45,725
You hire a personal trainer

67
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:48,394
because it's the only possible
way to get yourself to do it.

68
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:49,895
So you think he lied
about the trip?

69
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:51,772
Well, I'm almost certain.

70
00:03:52,314 --> 00:03:54,150
So if he's not white-water
rafting, where is he?

71
00:03:54,316 --> 00:03:56,235
Well, I don't know, but I'm sure
you two will figure it out.

72
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:57,570
And, Rigsby...

73
00:03:58,487 --> 00:04:00,322
Put the cupcake back.

74
00:04:21,784 --> 00:04:24,912
"Lisbon, I can hear you skulking
around out there. What is it?"

75
00:04:25,037 --> 00:04:28,207
We've got a case.
You can deal with Red John later.

76
00:04:28,332 --> 00:04:31,251
Yeah, Missy Roberts.
I already broke that wide open.

77
00:04:31,377 --> 00:04:34,380
Yeah, I heard.
The old rafting trip gambit?

78
00:04:34,505 --> 00:04:36,256
Yep, exactly.

79
00:04:36,382 --> 00:04:38,926
{\an8}Except for Kip Roberts
texted a picture of himself

80
00:04:39,051 --> 00:04:41,095
{\an8}to Missy right before she died.

81
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:44,973
{\an8}He's holding a paddle next
to a river with a raft full of bozos.

82
00:04:45,933 --> 00:04:47,434
Trick photography.

83
00:04:47,559 --> 00:04:49,311
{\an8}The Tahoe cops are gonna
go pick him up

84
00:04:49,436 --> 00:04:52,398
{\an8}but in the meantime, let's go
talk to the victim's sister.

85
00:04:56,443 --> 00:04:58,195
{\an8}Jane, I need you.

86
00:05:15,462 --> 00:05:16,964
{\an8}It's nice to be needed.

87
00:05:19,341 --> 00:05:20,968
{\an8}Anything for you, Lisbon.

88
00:05:25,431 --> 00:05:27,516
{\an8}We're very sorry for your loss, Emma.

89
00:05:27,683 --> 00:05:29,601
{\an8}Were you and your sister close?

90
00:05:29,727 --> 00:05:31,854
{\an8}Missy was like
a second mother to me but...

91
00:05:32,646 --> 00:05:35,816
{\an8}you know, now we're just...
in different places in our lives

92
00:05:35,941 --> 00:05:38,193
{\an8}so I just hadn't seen her
in a while.

93
00:05:38,318 --> 00:05:40,738
{\an8}Did she say if she was having
any problems recently?

94
00:05:41,238 --> 00:05:44,241
{\an8}I knew that she was tired
of... staying at home

95
00:05:44,366 --> 00:05:46,452
{\an8}you know, and...and, like,
not feeling useful

96
00:05:46,577 --> 00:05:51,290
{\an8}and I think that that was why
she started volunteering... at the bakery.

97
00:05:51,582 --> 00:05:55,252
{\an8}- Where?
- The O.G. Bakery.

98
00:05:55,377 --> 00:05:57,254
{\an8}It's this nonprofit
where they...

99
00:05:57,379 --> 00:06:01,175
{\an8}They teach ex-cons new skills,
you know like baking and...

100
00:06:01,633 --> 00:06:04,428
{\an8}She started there
a few months ago.

101
00:06:04,595 --> 00:06:06,430
Was anybody giving her
trouble there?

102
00:06:07,931 --> 00:06:11,769
{\an8}- Not that I know of.
- Were Missy and Kip, uh...

103
00:06:11,977 --> 00:06:14,271
{\an8}Trying anything
to save their marriage?

104
00:06:14,897 --> 00:06:16,815
{\an8}About a month ago, they...

105
00:06:17,399 --> 00:06:20,736
{\an8}went on this radio show
with this Love Doctor guy and...

106
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:23,697
I think they were seeing him
privately also.

107
00:06:23,822 --> 00:06:25,532
A love doctor, huh?

108
00:06:26,033 --> 00:06:29,286
{\an8}Some... Buddy... something,
I don't know.

109
00:06:30,370 --> 00:06:32,539
- Henner or...
- Buddy Hennings?

110
00:06:33,123 --> 00:06:37,795
{\an8}He has a talk radio show... "Prescription
For Love with Buddy Hennings".

111
00:06:38,670 --> 00:06:42,007
{\an8}What? I've listened to it
in my car a few times.

112
00:06:42,132 --> 00:06:44,885
All right. I'll go talk
to Buddy Hennings

113
00:06:45,052 --> 00:06:48,055
{\an8}the Love Doctor, and you
check out the shady bakery.

114
00:06:48,180 --> 00:06:51,183
Van Pelt and Rigsby can handle that.
I'll go to the radio station with you.

115
00:06:51,308 --> 00:06:54,853
- Ahh... that's 'cause you're a fan.
- I am not!

116
00:06:54,978 --> 00:06:57,105
Look, I just think
he's a viable lead.

117
00:06:57,231 --> 00:06:59,525
It's all right, Lisbon.
We all have our guilty pleasures.

118
00:07:06,990 --> 00:07:10,661
{\an8}- Oh, this must be very exciting for you.
- That's enough.

119
00:07:13,038 --> 00:07:14,665
Hey, Van Pelt.
What'd you find out?

120
00:07:14,790 --> 00:07:17,835
Turns out one of the ex-cons
at the bakery was still selling drugs...

121
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:20,045
a girl named Monica Suarez, 20.

122
00:07:20,170 --> 00:07:22,798
Missy found out and reported her
to the bakery supervisor.

123
00:07:23,006 --> 00:07:24,383
Well, what's Monica's deal?

124
00:07:24,508 --> 00:07:26,385
"She's been in the system
since she was 14."

125
00:07:26,510 --> 00:07:28,720
Vandalism, assault, dealing.

126
00:07:28,846 --> 00:07:30,597
She just got out of Chowchilla
six months ago.

127
00:07:30,722 --> 00:07:31,932
Ah. Real sweetheart.

128
00:07:32,057 --> 00:07:34,309
"Yeah, that's what the bakery
supervisor said."

129
00:07:34,476 --> 00:07:37,563
After Missy reported Monica,
Missy's tires were slashed.

130
00:07:37,729 --> 00:07:39,815
She said she saw Monica
following her around a few times.

131
00:07:39,940 --> 00:07:41,483
All right, you and Riggs
go and pick her up.

132
00:07:41,608 --> 00:07:42,818
All right.

133
00:07:49,366 --> 00:07:50,826
"They're celebrating the opening..."

134
00:07:50,951 --> 00:07:53,453
Hi. We need to speak
with Buddy Hennings.

135
00:07:54,288 --> 00:07:55,706
If you want to be on the show

136
00:07:55,831 --> 00:07:58,917
you have to fill out this form
and take it to couples-intake.

137
00:07:59,585 --> 00:08:01,795
Oh, we're not a couple.
Please.

138
00:08:02,212 --> 00:08:05,048
What she means is ours is
more of a platonic love.

139
00:08:08,510 --> 00:08:10,220
Buddy Hennings, please.

140
00:08:10,929 --> 00:08:13,682
He's on the air.
Talk to his producer.

141
00:08:14,141 --> 00:08:17,811
She's a huge fan.
She's a little... very excited. Yeah.

142
00:08:19,271 --> 00:08:23,567
Sean, what I'm hearing from you
is that Lisa has become sexually cold

143
00:08:23,692 --> 00:08:25,652
ever since the baby was born.

144
00:08:25,777 --> 00:08:28,488
Oh, excuse me. This...this isn't
a good time. Can I help you?

145
00:08:28,614 --> 00:08:30,657
I'm Agent Lisbon
with the CBI.

146
00:08:30,782 --> 00:08:32,326
- This is Patrick Jane.
- Hi.

147
00:08:32,451 --> 00:08:35,996
We're investigating the murder
of Missy Roberts.

148
00:08:36,121 --> 00:08:38,749
I'm... I'm sorry to hear about
that, but we're live here.

149
00:08:38,957 --> 00:08:40,542
Come here, please.

150
00:08:40,667 --> 00:08:42,169
You have to excuse
our producer Gary.

151
00:08:42,294 --> 00:08:45,797
He's a bit of a control freak.
Thinks everyone's out to ruin his show.

152
00:08:46,048 --> 00:08:48,759
Well, just 'cause he's paranoid
doesn't mean they're not out to get him.

153
00:08:48,884 --> 00:08:50,844
- Who are you?
- I'm Elizabeth Hennings.

154
00:08:50,969 --> 00:08:52,930
- Hi.
- I'm Buddy's wife and manager.

155
00:08:53,263 --> 00:08:56,058
Uh, we heard about Missy.
It's just awful.

156
00:08:56,183 --> 00:08:57,684
We need to talk to Buddy.

157
00:08:57,809 --> 00:08:59,478
Okay, well, it's gonna be
a little while, all right?

158
00:08:59,603 --> 00:09:00,687
'Cause we're in the middle
of a segment

159
00:09:00,812 --> 00:09:02,564
then we have to shoot
a promo for a Webcast, so...

160
00:09:02,689 --> 00:09:05,275
That's all right. We like to watch.
Don't we?

161
00:09:05,943 --> 00:09:08,153
look at each other in the eye.

162
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:10,489
- Look at this. Look at this.
- Please don't touch anything.

163
00:09:10,614 --> 00:09:11,657
No, I won't.

164
00:09:17,746 --> 00:09:19,164
Thank you, Mr. Lewis.

165
00:09:19,831 --> 00:09:22,084
Monica's parole officer said
it's the right address.

166
00:09:23,043 --> 00:09:26,380
- So we keep waiting.
- Yup.

167
00:09:30,467 --> 00:09:32,302
Stakeouts are the worst.

168
00:09:35,055 --> 00:09:36,682
Wayne, is something wrong?

169
00:09:40,060 --> 00:09:42,771
No. There's nothing wrong. I...

170
00:09:44,314 --> 00:09:46,817
I've been feeling kinda weird
since you've been back.

171
00:09:46,984 --> 00:09:48,944
Yeah, you've been acting
kind of weird.

172
00:09:49,069 --> 00:09:50,946
- What's up with that?
- It's just...

173
00:09:51,613 --> 00:09:53,991
When you were in L.A.,
I had time to think...

174
00:09:54,116 --> 00:09:59,746
- About you. About us.
- Okay. And?

175
00:10:00,288 --> 00:10:02,749
Well, I mean,
did you think about me at all?

176
00:10:02,874 --> 00:10:04,292
Of course I did.

177
00:10:10,632 --> 00:10:11,675
Yeah...

178
00:10:11,967 --> 00:10:13,635
Wait...
is that her on the left?

179
00:10:18,348 --> 00:10:19,683
Uh, yeah. Come on.

180
00:10:21,643 --> 00:10:22,853
Monica Suarez?

181
00:10:24,813 --> 00:10:26,064
Hey!

182
00:10:28,692 --> 00:10:29,818
CBI!

183
00:10:30,569 --> 00:10:32,029
Get out of the way!
Police!

184
00:10:39,411 --> 00:10:40,454
Police!

185
00:10:51,339 --> 00:10:52,382
Come here.

186
00:10:52,507 --> 00:10:54,551
Get your hands off me!
I got nothing on me!

187
00:10:54,676 --> 00:10:57,179
Yeah, 'cause you threw
your stash in the dumpster.

188
00:10:59,473 --> 00:11:01,516
- You good?
- Yeah, you?

189
00:11:01,641 --> 00:11:02,684
Yeah.

190
00:11:03,894 --> 00:11:05,562
Talk to me
about Missy Roberts.

191
00:11:05,937 --> 00:11:08,857
- Who?
- She was murdered last night.

192
00:11:09,733 --> 00:11:11,109
First I heard of it.

193
00:11:11,318 --> 00:11:13,487
But you messed with her
when she got you fired, right?

194
00:11:13,904 --> 00:11:16,573
I was still on parole.
I... I needed that job.

195
00:11:16,698 --> 00:11:18,700
So you slashed her tires,
stalked her?

196
00:11:18,867 --> 00:11:21,244
I... I just followed her around,
you know, to freak her out.

197
00:11:21,369 --> 00:11:23,413
Oh, yeah?
You see anything interesting?

198
00:11:24,456 --> 00:11:26,333
Not really. I mean, you know,
she went shoe shopping

199
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:29,252
and got mani-pedis a lot...
you know, rich lady stuff.

200
00:11:29,377 --> 00:11:34,674
- Where were you last night?
- I was at my cousin's quinceañera.

201
00:11:37,135 --> 00:11:40,180
- All night.
- All right. Come on.

202
00:11:41,139 --> 00:11:42,390
Let's go!

203
00:11:43,266 --> 00:11:46,353
"This is Buddy Hennings with
Prescription For Love."

204
00:11:46,478 --> 00:11:49,397
"We'll be back in ten minutes,
right after the news."

205
00:11:59,407 --> 00:12:03,537
Buddy, these people are from CBI.
They're, uh, here about Missy.

206
00:12:04,121 --> 00:12:06,915
Buddy Hennings.
Glad to help any way I can.

207
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:10,127
Buddy, we have a phone call
with the publisher in about a half hour.

208
00:12:10,252 --> 00:12:13,130
- So, if you all don't need me...
- Oh, by all means.

209
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:17,926
I know you're a busy man.
We just have a few questions.

210
00:12:18,051 --> 00:12:20,846
Missy and Kip... they were
on your show a while back?

211
00:12:20,971 --> 00:12:23,306
Yes. Good people, both of them.

212
00:12:23,765 --> 00:12:27,602
Some of the couples we get in here
they're really just here for their 15 minutes

213
00:12:27,727 --> 00:12:31,940
but I had a feeling that Missy
really wanted to work on her marriage.

214
00:12:32,065 --> 00:12:33,859
That's why I offered
to see them privately.

215
00:12:33,984 --> 00:12:36,153
And when was the last time
you saw them?

216
00:12:36,278 --> 00:12:38,113
Last week. Thursday.

217
00:12:38,697 --> 00:12:40,907
Supposed to come in this week,
but she called to cancel.

218
00:12:41,032 --> 00:12:42,617
She didn't give a reason.

219
00:12:44,744 --> 00:12:47,664
You know what? I have to take this.
Excuse me. I'm sorry.

220
00:12:49,249 --> 00:12:50,876
Well, listen, Buddy,
while we're just chatting

221
00:12:51,001 --> 00:12:53,295
just you and I here,
hanging out, a couple of guys

222
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:57,424
- do you think Kip could have done it?
- No. Absolutely not.

223
00:12:57,549 --> 00:13:00,635
But you said it was Missy that wanted
help with their marriage, not Kip.

224
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:03,763
Well, I think in the beginning
he was going along to get along

225
00:13:03,889 --> 00:13:07,058
- but he turned a corner.
- How so?

226
00:13:07,642 --> 00:13:10,312
Well, in the first few sessions
he was very distant

227
00:13:10,437 --> 00:13:12,731
very uncooperative,
both with me and with Missy.

228
00:13:13,773 --> 00:13:15,650
But then, after
a couple of sessions

229
00:13:15,775 --> 00:13:20,071
he developed an attentiveness and a warmth
that I hadn't seen in him before.

230
00:13:20,197 --> 00:13:22,365
- He really changed.
